# loop-budget.md — {{ project.name }}

Token cost is the loop failure that does not announce itself. A loop retrying a hopeless goal
every night costs real money and produces nothing, and it looks exactly like a loop working.

| Scope | Ceiling | On breach |
|---|---|---|
| Single attempt | 120k tokens | abandon attempt, log, next |
| Single goal | 600k tokens | halt, checkpoint `STATE.md`, escalate |
| One scheduled run | 1.2M tokens | halt run |
| Rolling 7 days | 6M tokens | circuit breaker opens |

## Cost drivers, in order

1. **Model-judged gates.** If any of them read images, vision tokens dominate everything else.
   Run them once per goal at the end, never per attempt.
2. **Re-reading the repository each attempt.** `STATE.md` plus the failing gate text is the
   whole brief. Do not paste the tree.
3. **The no-progress spin.** Three identical failures is not persistence. The stop rule in
   `gate.yaml` exists purely to cap this.

## Circuit breaker

State in `.loop/breaker.json`. Opens on a rolling ceiling breach, three consecutive
escalations, or any denylist touch. Closes only by human action — no automatic half-open
state, because a loop that decides on its own that it is healthy again defeats the purpose.

## Instrument before you tune

Do not set these from intuition. `loop-run-log.md` records what each run actually cost. Tune
after ten real runs, not before.
